One further heartbreak:  no photo!  The last 6 or 7 constructors have quite charming pix on xwordinfo, and for me it's often the cherry on top of the treat...  The wit and creativity shine through.
"People we'd like to know!"

@Mean Old Lady
Yep. Endless dialog. 

I was so happy when unlimited texting came along at a reasonable price. I have family who would never communicate otherwise.

@Keith Adams

They do have cryptics. Every 8 weeks. Tha last one was July 5. You can’t get them on the NYT site or app, but if you join xwordinfo.com, you can solve online. 

You can also solve in the paper if you want to buy them, but I think after 4 puzzles, it’s cheaper to pay for xwordinfo. Plus you can do the archive.

@Eva H.
You weren't very specific about why you thought the clues were terrible, but I'm seeing other complaints here that one [clue] or another isn't a synonym or the best definition for [answer]. 

Sunday clues are generally going to be a mix of easy-to-get and stretch-your-brain-to-find-the-connection. Every one of these clues, IMO, is fair. You have to think about some of them to get there. That's as it should be for a Sunday.

@Captain Quahog
My seemingly innocuous reply to you was quarantined 
I only wondered why no one mentioned _rusty in his _lown car. And if the title to the puzzle was a known saying in the world of the Simpsons?

@HeathieJ
Yep. I have found that what is going on with me dramatically affects my perception of puzzles. When I solve them late at night after a hard day, for instance, I almost always think they weren't humorous or clever. Just unnecessarily opaque. 

Unless it just so happens that the ones I've solved at night happened to be subpar? Maybe I have ESP that way.

@HeathieJ,

I’m kind of the same way about clues that reference other clues. They’re just annoying anymore. I used to race to the referred clue with anticipation to figure it out, now I just grimace and resolutely skip over it, thinking I’ll get to it when I get to it. It breaks my flow and rhythm and any momentum I’ve built up. 

Hope you get some rest and feel better soon. 🙏🏻

@NYC Traveler

Thank you, NYC Traveler! I appreciate it! 

And I appreciate your fellowship in disliking those reference clues. I think I'm going to follow suit and just ignore them until I have to deal with them. ☺️

@maryam
Barry and others can describe the convention more precisely than I can, but there are some acronyms and abbreviations that don't need to be indicated in the clue. I think one instance is if an acronym is more familiar than what it represents. 

On the main Games page is a link to How To Solve the New York Times Crossword. It has a ton of information and might be worth a read. <a href="https://www.nytimes.com/article/how-to-solve-a-crossword-puzzle.html" target="_blank">https://www.nytimes.com/article/how-to-solve-a-crossword-puzzle.html</a>

